# GPAW Library Installation Guide

This guide provides step-by-step instructions for building the required libraries for GPAW (Gaussian Projected Augmented Wave). These libraries are built with **Intel oneAPI 2025.3** and MPI support.

---

## Prerequisites

- **Intel oneAPI 2025.3** (verified in paths)
- **Intel MPI** (compatible with oneAPI)
- **Linux** (Ubuntu 22.04 or CentOS 8+ recommended)
- **Build environment**: `bash` and standard build tools

> 💡 *Note: GCC is optional - Intel compilers are preferred for optimal performance*

---

## Installation Procedure

Follow these steps **in order** to build all dependencies:

### 1. FFTW3 (Foundation Library)

```bash
# Configure environment for FFTW3
export FC="mpiifx -fc=ifx"
export F77=$FC
export CC="mpiicx -cc=icx"
export CXX=icpx
export MPICC="mpiicx -cc=icx"
export CPP="icx -E"
export FFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX512"
export CFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX512"

# Build FFTW3 with MPI and shared libraries
./configure --prefix=/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/fftw_build --enable-mpi --enable-shared
```

### 2. ELPA (Eigenvalue Solver)

```bash
# Configure environment for ELPA
export FC=mpiifx
export F90=$FC
export CC=mpiicx
export CXX=mpiicpx
export CPP="icx -E"
export FCFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX512 -fPIC -qopenmp"
export CFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX512 -fPIC -qopenmp"
export CXXFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX512 -fPIC -qopenmp"

export SCALAPACK_FCFLAGS="-I/home/skumar1/intel/oneapi/mkl/2025.3/include"
export SCALAPACK_LDFLAGS="-qmkl=cluster"

# Build ELPA with shared libraries (disable MPI module)
./configure --prefix=/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/elpa_build --enable-shared --disable-mpi-module
```

### 3. LIBVDWXC (Van der Waals Correction)

```bash
# Configure environment for LIBVDWXC (reuses FFTW3 settings)
export FC="mpiifx -fc=ifx"
export F77=$FC
export CC="mpiicx -cc=icx"
export CXX=icpx
export MPICC="mpiicx -cc=icx"
export CPP="icx -E"
export FFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX512"
export MPI_FCFLAGS=$FFLAGS
export CFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX512"
export MPI_CFLAGS=$CFLAGS
export CXXFLAGS=$CFLAGS

export LDFLAGS="-qmkl=cluster"
export FFTW3_INCLUDES="-I/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/fftw_build/include"
export FFTW3_LIBS="-L/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/fftw_build/lib -lfftw3 -lfftw3_mpi"

# Build LIBVDWXC with MPI and shared libraries
./configure --prefix=/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/libvdwxc_build --with-mpi --enable-shared
```

### 4. LIBXC (Exchange-Correlation Library)

```bash
# Configure environment for LIBXC
export FC=mpiifx
export CC=mpiicx
export CXX=mpiicpx
export FCFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX2"
export CFLAGS="-O2 -xCORE-AVX2"
export LDFLAGS="-qmkl=cluster"

# Build LIBXC with shared libraries and Fortran support
./configure --prefix=/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/libxc_build --enable-shared --enable-fortran
```

> ⚠️ **Critical Note**: All paths in this guide are specific to the user's environment (`/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/`).  
> **Customize these paths** to match your system configuration.

