## GPAW Site Configuration

For proper integration with GPAW, add this configuration to your `siteconfig.py`:

```python
import os

# Enable all required libraries
mpi = True
compiler = 'mpiicx'
scalapack = True
fftw = True
elpa = True
libxc = True
libvdwxc = True

# MKL libraries
libraries = [
    'mkl_scalapack_lp64',
    'mkl_blacs_intelmpi_lp6as',
    'mkl_intel_lp64',
    'mkl_sequential',
    'mkl_core',
    'mpi',
    'mkl_rt',
    'xc',
    'elpa',
    'vdwxc'
]

# Library paths
library_dirs = [
    os.environ['MKLROOT'] + '/lib/',
    os.environ['I_MPI_ROOT'] + '/lib/',
    '/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/libxc_build/lib',
    '/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/elpa_build/lib',
    '/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/fftw_build/lib',
    '/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/libvdwxc_build/lib'
]

# Include paths
include_dirs = [
    os.environ['MKLROOT'] + '/include',
    os.environ['I_MPI_ROOT'] + '/include',
    '/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/libxc_build/include',
    '/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/elpa_build/include/elpa-2025.01.002',
    '/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/fftw_build/include',
    '/home/skumar1/Apps/LIBS/GPAW/libvdwxc_build/include'
]

# Compiler flags
extra_compile_args = ['-O2', '-fPIC', '-qmkl=cluster', '-xCORE-AVX512']
extra_link_args = ['-qopenmp']
```

> 🔧 **Important**: Replace all paths with your actual installation locations.

